   1728  fafe							; ========================================================================
   1729  fafe							; BombMarkWalls (S5.2, moved from bank0) — pinned at $FB10.
   1730  fafe							;   On the bomb 1->2 edge: walk the rect cache, set WallMask bit (BombPacked
   1731  fafe							;   b3-6) for each w==2 rect whose x is in blast cols (bomb left-half col
   1732  fafe							;   +-2, clamped 0..19). w==2 = one D7 logical cell (rect x/w are emitted
   1733  fafe							;   in 4px display cols; a thin wall is exactly one cell = 2 cols). Skip x==0 (screen border). Score is NOT done here —
   1734  fafe							;   pads cannot nest (ReturnPad switches to bank0), so this returns
   1735  fafe							;   A = #walls newly broken and the bank0 caller adds +75 per wall.
   1736  fafe							;   Plan 5.1: each newly broken rect is punched here immediately —
   1737  fafe							;   ClearPFColumn on col x AND col x+1 (D7 thin wall w = 2 display cols;
   1738  fafe							;   the single-col punch left half the wall standing behind a set mask bit)
   1739  fafe							;   — the old VBL ApplyBombWalls re-apply + EnterRoom
   1740  fafe							;   restore are deleted (D1-B). WallMask b3-6 survives only in-room: the
   1741  fafe							;   hot parent-mask AND (HotOverlapBody) still reads it until phase 6.
   1742  fafe							;   ABW tables + BombMaskBit are bank1-only now (kernel copies died with
   1743  fafe							;   ApplyBombWalls).
   1744  fafe							;   #7(i): walk now covers rects 0-4 (cache slot rect4 at $DC-$DF was
   1745  fafe							;   loaded but never walked — a thin wall there was unbreakable). Rect5
   1746  fafe							;   is not cached (ZP ends $DF) and stays unwalkable — shipped models
   1747  fafe							;   have no thin rect at idx5. Rect idx4 has no WallMask bit: PairGone's
   1748  fafe							;   buffer read replaces the mask as its double-score guard. A full
   1749  fafe							;   buffer cell-sweep was evaluated and REJECTED: find_rectangles merges
   1750  fafe							;   maximal runs, so every shipped thin wall has a solid neighbor slab
   1751  fafe							;   (checked all 8 models) — buffer adjacency cannot distinguish thin
   1752  fafe							;   stubs from thick walls without breaking gameplay parity.
   1753  fafe							;   Also fixed: the col x+1 punch passed the ABW table VALUE (the rect's
   1754  fafe							;   ZP address) as the ClearPFColumn col instead of deref'ing rect.x —
   1755  fafe							;   the second half of every thin wall was punched at a garbage col
   1756  fafe							;   (caught by the new test_bomb_strip rect-walk case; pre-existing
   1757  fafe							;   since plan 5.1). RcBase is now clamped ≤5 at the bank2 cache load —
   1758  fafe							;   BMW trusts it (no local clamp).
